      "math_academy_id": "q-105398",
      "knowledge_point_id": "77673d0c-9f03-5915-b2ab-4a5d6cb2d94d",
      "knowledge_point": "Inverting a Frobenius Matrix",
      "problem": "Find the inverse of the following matrix:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that we're given a Frobenius matrix:\n\n- all entries on the main diagonal are ones\n\n- the matrix has only one column (the $2$nd column) where some entries below the main diagonal are not zeros\n\n- all the other entries outside the main diagonal are zeros\n\nTo find the inverse of a Frobenius matrix, we simply take the non-zero entries outside the main diagonal with opposite signs. \n\nIn our case, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
